{ "The gap between your previous employment in Australia and your current employment in the UK is not a problem for an intra-company transfer visa. The visa requires that you have been employed by the same company for at least three years in the last nine years, and that you are being transferred to the UK to work for the same company. The fact that you have a gap between your employment in Australia and your current employment in the UK does not affect your eligibility for the visa. You can still apply for an intra-company transfer visa as long as you meet the other eligibility requirements. You will need to provide evidence of your previous employment with the company in Australia, as well as evidence of your current employment with the company in the UK. You will also need to provide a certificate of sponsorship from your employer in the UK, which confirms that they are sponsoring your application for a visa. You should check the UK government's website for the most up-to-date information on the eligibility requirements and application process for an intra-company transfer visa. ":

